hanzidraw bundles no third-party data. At first run it downloads the following
open datasets into the user data directory:

Make Me a Hanzi — stroke medians and outlines
  https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi
  Derived from Arphic Technology's AR PL UMing and AR PL UKai fonts, used under
  the Arphic Public License; the project's own code and derived data are under
  the LGPL. Attribution retained per those licences.

hanziDB — character frequency ranks, pinyin readings, stroke counts
  https://github.com/ruddfawcett/hanziDB.csv

CC-CEDICT — Chinese-English dictionary, used here for word/phrase pinyin keys
  https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict
  Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).

rime-essay (optional) — word frequency table used to rank phrase candidates
  https://github.com/rime/rime-essay
